# Server Benchmarks

A benchmark suite which, transparently, stress-tests web servers and generates reports in Markdown, CSV, JSON and SVG charts. It measures requests per second, latency, data transfer and total completion time.

## Why

Most benchmark suites don't test real-life applications. This suite runs each framework's application as a self-contained program and measures it with a trusted third-party HTTP load generator, [bombardier](https://github.com/codesenberg/bombardier), which acts as a real HTTP client — one more reason of transparency. [Contributions](CONTRIBUTING.md) and improvements are always welcome.

## Installation

The only requirement for the benchmark tool itself is the [Go Programming Language](https://go.dev/dl/).

```sh
go install github.com/kataras/server-benchmarks@latest
go install github.com/codesenberg/bombardier@latest
```

Depending on the test cases you run, you may also need [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) and the [.NET SDK](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download).

## How to run

1. Navigate to the directory that contains your **tests.yml** file
2. Run `server-benchmarks`
3. Open the generated **RESULTS.md** file

Useful variants:

```sh
# run only specific tests or environments:
server-benchmarks run -t rest -t static.iris

# custom spec file, output directory and settle time between runs:
server-benchmarks run -i ./tests.dev.yml -o ./dev -wait-run 3s

# list the tests of a spec without running anything:
server-benchmarks list

# re-render the reports (Markdown, CSV, SVG) of a previous run:
server-benchmarks export -i ./results.json -o ./
```

### Run using Docker

```sh
docker build -t server-benchmarks .
docker run --rm -v ${PWD}:/data server-benchmarks
```

